"""
## Purpose and audience
Purpose: Pin how a line of Arabic or Devanagari text sizes its line box when the
primary font (Liberation Sans) lacks the script and a fallback face draws it.
Audience: web renderer inline layout / line-box maintainers.

Chrome rule (Blink, `line-height: normal`): the line box takes the UNION of the
primary font's strut and every face the run actually uses. Each face gives its
own ascent and descent (rounded at the used size, device size at k > 1) plus
half its line gap. With a fixed `line-height`, only the strut counts.

Chrome oracle (Chrome for Testing 159, `--headless=new --disable-gpu
--hide-scrollbars --window-size=400,300`, `--force-device-scale-factor` 1 and 4).
Body `font:16px 'Liberation Sans', 'Noto Sans Arabic', 'Noto Sans Devanagari'`:
the two Noto faces are the bundled files, loaded with `@font-face`. Simple's page
names Liberation Sans and picks the same Noto files from `lang`.

| block                          | k=1 rows | k=4 rows | DOM height k=1 / k=4 |
|--------------------------------|----------|----------|----------------------|
| `lang=ar` مرحبا بالعالم         | 30..63   | 120..254 | 34 / 33.75           |
| Latin `Hxgl`                   | 64..81   | 255..328 | 18 / 18.5            |
| `lang=hi` हिंदी                 | 82..102  | 329..413 | 21 / 21.25           |
| Latin `Hxgl`                   | 103..120 | 414..487 | 18 / 18.5            |

Face metrics, from hhea (ascent / descent / line gap, per 1000 em):
- Liberation Sans: 905 / 212 / 33. At 16 px that is 14 / 3, gap 1, so line 18 and
  baseline 14. At 64 px it is 58 / 14, gap 2, so line 74 and baseline 59.
- Noto Sans Arabic: 1374 / 738 / 0. At 16 px that is 22 / 12; at 64 px, 88 / 47.
- Noto Sans Devanagari: 896 / 408 / 0. At 16 px that is 14 / 7; at 64 px, 57 / 26.

So the Arabic line is 22 + 12 = 34 (88 + 47 = 135 at k=4), with its baseline 22
below the line top (88 at k=4). The Devanagari line is 14 + 7 = 21 (59 + 26 = 85
at k=4), with its baseline on the strut (14, and 59 at k=4).

A wrapped Arabic paragraph of 4 lines is 4 x 34 = 136 (4 x 33.75 = 135 at k=4).
An underline (`text-decoration-color:#0f0`) sits at the run's own baseline + 1:
Latin 45, Arabic 91, Devanagari 137 at k=1 (183, 366, 552 at k=4, 6 rows thick).
The same holds for the primary face: a DejaVu Sans underline is one row lower
than a Liberation Sans one (ascent 15 vs 14), a Liberation Mono one a row higher.
With a fixed line-height the glyphs still hang from the strut baseline: k=4 ink of
a `line-height:20px` Arabic block is 136..206 and of a `1.5` one 544..614.
A `line-height:40px` Devanagari block is exactly 40 tall, the same as Latin: no
union.

The ink-edge checks (Chrome Arabic 41..57 / 162..232, Devanagari 82..97 /
330..396) live in `glyph_vertical_raster_phase_chrome159_spec.spl`: with the
line box right, one edge per run differs by one raster row there.
Ink is any pixel whose three channels are all under 90, between x 20 and 300 CSS
px. Chrome's ink rows: Arabic 41..57 at k=1 and 162..232 at k=4; Devanagari 82..97
at k=1 and 330..396 at k=4.
"""
"""
Traceability: REQ-WEB-LINEBOX-USED-FONTS-001 — a line-height:normal line box holds every face its text uses.
"""
# @tag: unit, browser_engine, layout, text, chrome159
# @cover src/lib/gc_async_mut/gpu/browser_engine/simple_web_html_layout_renderer_layout_foundation.spl 1%
use std.spec.*
use std.gc_async_mut.gpu.browser_engine.simple_web_layout_engine2d_fast.{
    simple_web_layout_render_html_pixels_engine2d_at_device_scale
}

val CSS_W: i32 = 400
val CSS_H: i32 = 300

val STACK: text = "<!doctype html><html lang=\"en\"><body style=\"margin:0;background:#fff;font:16px Liberation Sans;color:#000\"><div style=\"position:absolute;left:20px;top:30px;width:300px\"><div lang=ar style=\"background:#f00\">مرحبا بالعالم</div><div style=\"background:#0f0\">Hxgl</div><div lang=hi style=\"background:#00f\">हिंदी</div><div style=\"background:#ff0\">Hxgl</div></div></body></html>"

val WRAP: text = "<!doctype html><html lang=\"en\"><body style=\"margin:0;background:#fff;font:16px Liberation Sans;color:#000\"><div style=\"position:absolute;left:20px;top:30px;width:300px\"><div lang=ar style=\"background:#f00;width:70px\">مرحبا بالعالم مرحبا بالعالم</div><div style=\"background:#0f0\">Hxgl</div><div lang=hi style=\"background:#00f;line-height:40px\">हिंदी</div><div style=\"background:#ff0\">Hxgl</div></div></body></html>"

val UNDERLINE: text = "<!doctype html><html lang=\"en\"><body style=\"margin:0;background:#fff;font:16px Liberation Sans;color:#000\"><div style=\"position:absolute;left:20px;top:30px;width:300px;text-decoration:underline;text-decoration-color:#0f0\"><div lang=en>Hxgl Hxgl</div><div lang=ar style=\"margin-top:20px\">مرحبا بالعالم</div><div lang=hi style=\"margin-top:20px\">हिंदी हिंदी</div></div></body></html>"
val UNDERLINE_FACES: text = "<!doctype html><html lang=\"en\"><body style=\"margin:0;background:#fff;font:16px Liberation Sans;color:#000\"><div style=\"position:absolute;left:20px;top:30px;width:300px;text-decoration:underline;text-decoration-color:#0f0\"><div style=\"font-family:DejaVu Sans\">Hxgl Hxgl</div><div style=\"margin-top:20px;font-family:Liberation Serif\">Hxgl Hxgl</div><div style=\"margin-top:20px;font-family:Liberation Mono\">Hxgl Hxgl</div><div style=\"margin-top:20px;font-family:DejaVu Sans;font-size:40px\">Hxgl</div></div></body></html>"
val FIXED_LH: text = "<!doctype html><html lang=\"en\"><body style=\"margin:0;background:#fff;font:16px Liberation Sans;color:#000\"><div style=\"position:absolute;left:20px;top:30px;width:300px;text-decoration:underline;text-decoration-color:#0f0\"><div lang=ar style=\"line-height:20px\">مرحبا بالعالم</div><div lang=hi style=\"margin-top:20px;line-height:40px\">हिंदी हिंदी</div><div lang=ar style=\"margin-top:20px;line-height:1.5\">مرحبا بالعالم</div></div></body></html>"

fn _render(page: text, k: i32) -> [u32]:
    simple_web_layout_render_html_pixels_engine2d_at_device_scale(page, CSS_W, CSS_H, k, "cpu_simd")

# Non-white colour runs down the column at CSS x 300, as `a..b` device rows.
fn _blocks(px: [u32], k: i32) -> text:
    val w = CSS_W * k
    val h = CSS_H * k
    if px.len() != (w * h) as i64:
        return "empty frame"
    val cx = 300 * k
    var out = ""
    var prev: u32 = 0xFFFFFFu32
    var start = 0
    var y = 0
    while y <= h:
        val p = if y < h: px[y * w + cx] & 0xFFFFFFu32 else: 0xFFFFFFu32
        if p != prev:
            if prev != 0xFFFFFFu32:
                out = if out == "": "{start}..{y - 1}" else: out + " {start}..{y - 1}"
            prev = p
            start = y
        y = y + 1
    out

# Device row runs holding green (#0f0-ish) pixels, x in [20k, 320k).
fn _green_rows(px: [u32], k: i32) -> text:
    val w = CSS_W * k
    val h = CSS_H * k
    if px.len() != (w * h) as i64:
        return "empty frame"
    var out = ""
    var start = -1
    var y = 0
    while y <= h:
        var g = false
        if y < h:
            var x = 20 * k
            while x < 320 * k and not g:
                val q = px[y * w + x]
                g = ((q >> 8u32) & 0xFFu32) > 150u32 and ((q >> 16u32) & 0xFFu32) < 120u32 and (q & 0xFFu32) < 120u32
                x = x + 1
        if g and start < 0: start = y
        if not g and start >= 0:
            out = if out == "": "{start}..{y - 1}" else: out + " {start}..{y - 1}"
            start = -1
        y = y + 1
    out

# First and last device row with ink (all channels < 90) in rows y0..y1.
fn _ink_rows(px: [u32], k: i32, y0: i32, y1: i32) -> text:
    val w = CSS_W * k
    if px.len() != (w * CSS_H * k) as i64:
        return "empty frame"
    var i0 = -1
    var i1 = -1
    var y = y0
    while y <= y1:
        var x = 20 * k
        while x < 300 * k:
            val q = px[y * w + x]
            if ((q >> 16u32) & 0xFFu32) < 90u32 and ((q >> 8u32) & 0xFFu32) < 90u32 and (q & 0xFFu32) < 90u32:
                if i0 < 0: i0 = y
                i1 = y
            x = x + 1
        y = y + 1
    "{i0}..{i1}"

describe "line box of a fallback-face run (line-height: normal) against Chrome 159":
    it "AC-1: Arabic and Devanagari blocks take the fallback face's height at k=1":
        step("Chrome k=1 rows: Arabic 30..63, Latin 64..81, Devanagari 82..102, Latin 103..120")
        expect(_blocks(_render(STACK, 1), 1)).to_equal("30..63 64..81 82..102 103..120")

    it "AC-2: the same blocks at device scale 4":
        step("Chrome k=4 rows: 120..254 255..328 329..413 414..487")
        expect(_blocks(_render(STACK, 4), 4)).to_equal("120..254 255..328 329..413 414..487")

    it "AC-5: every line of a wrapped Arabic paragraph takes the union; a fixed line-height does not":
        step("Chrome: the 70px Arabic block (left of the x 300 column) ends at 166 (k=1) / 660 (k=4); the line-height:40px block stays 40 rows")
        expect(_blocks(_render(WRAP, 1), 1)).to_equal("166..183 184..223 224..241")
        expect(_blocks(_render(WRAP, 4), 4)).to_equal("660..733 734..893 894..967")

    it "AC-6: an underline sits below the run's own baseline, not the primary font's ascent":
        step("Chrome green underline rows: Latin 45, Arabic 91 (= 68 + 22 + 1), Devanagari 137 at k=1; 183..188 366..371 552..557 at k=4")
        expect(_green_rows(_render(UNDERLINE, 1), 1)).to_equal("45..45 91..91 137..137")
        expect(_green_rows(_render(UNDERLINE, 4), 4)).to_equal("183..188 366..371 552..557")

    it "AC-7: an underline hangs from its own primary face's ascent, not Liberation Sans's":
        step("Chrome 159: DejaVu Sans 46 (ascent 15), Liberation Serif 84, Liberation Mono 121 (ascent 13), DejaVu Sans 40px 184..187 at k=1")
        expect(_green_rows(_render(UNDERLINE_FACES, 1), 1)).to_equal("46..46 84..84 121..121 184..187")
        step("k=4, the three 16px faces: 182..187 336..341 484..489 (the 40px one, 737..752, is in glyph_vertical_raster_phase_chrome159_spec)")
        val k4 = _green_rows(_render(UNDERLINE_FACES, 4), 4).split(" ")
        expect(k4[0] + " " + k4[1] + " " + k4[2]).to_equal("182..187 336..341 484..489")

    it "AC-8: under a fixed line-height the Arabic glyphs still hang from the strut baseline":
        step("Chrome k=4 ink: line-height:20px block 136..206, line-height:1.5 block 544..614 (no union, but the run is shaped by Noto Sans Arabic)")
        val px = _render(FIXED_LH, 4)
        expect(_ink_rows(px, 4, 120, 300) + " " + _ink_rows(px, 4, 500, 700)).to_equal("136..206 544..614")
